direction: down

title: |md
  ## AF_XDP architecture and ownership
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

umem: "UMEM registration" {
  style.fill: "#dbeafe"
  body: |md
    **Does:**
    - userspace allocates frames
    - registers them with kernel

    **Why next:**
    - driver needs buffers for RX

    **State:**
    - FILL ring advertises
    - free UMEM frame addresses
  |
}

driver: "driver RX" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
  body: |md
    **Does:**
    - RX into driver buffers
    - zero-copy DMA to UMEM
    - copy mode copies into UMEM

    **Why next:**
    - XDP picks stack vs AF_XDP

    **State:**
    - packet is xdp_buff
  |
}

xdp: "XDP redirect" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
  body: |md
    **Does:**
    - bpf_redirect_map(
    - &xsks_map, qid, 0)
    - looks up queue socket

    **Why next:**
    - redirect gives ownership
    - to XSK RX ring, only if
    - a socket is registered

    **State:**
    - stack-bound or XSK-bound
  |
}

rings: "AF_XDP rings" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  body: |md
    **Does:** descriptors move
    kernel <-> user:
    - FILL gives free frames
    - RX gives received packets
    - TX submits sends
    - COMPLETION recycles TX

    **State:**
    - descriptors, not copies,
    - are fast-path currency
  |
}

user: "userspace poll loop" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  body: |md
    **Does:**
    - reads RX descriptors
    - processes UMEM data
    - returns addresses to FILL

    **Why next:**
    - without recycling, RX runs
    - out of buffers and drops

    **State:**
    - ownership returns to kernel
  |
}

umem -> driver: "free frame descriptors"
driver -> xdp: "packet in xdp_buff"
xdp -> rings: "XDP_REDIRECT to XSKMAP"
rings -> user: "RX descriptors"
user -> umem: "recycled frames"
